{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-proverbs-026",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 26,
  "title": "Proverbs 26",
  "display_title": "Proverbs 26",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "proverbs",
  "book": "Proverbs",
  "bookName": "Proverbs",
  "bookOrder": 20,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 26,
  "sortOrder": 20026,
  "verseCount": 28,
  "aliases": [
    "Prov",
    "Pr",
    "Prv"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "As snow in summer, and as rain in harvest, so honour is not seemly for a fool.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "As the bird by wandering, as the swallow by flying, so the curse causeless shall not come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "A whip for the horse, a bridle for the ass, and a rod for the fool’s back.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Answer not a fool according to his folly, lest thou also be like unto him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Answer a fool according to his folly, lest he be wise in his own conceit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "He that sendeth a message by the hand of a fool cutteth off the feet, and drinketh damage.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "The legs of the lame are not equal: so is a parable in the mouth of fools.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "As he that bindeth a stone in a sling, so is he that giveth honour to a fool.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "As a thorn goeth up into the hand of a drunkard, so is a parable in the mouth of fools.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "The great God that formed all things both rewardeth the fool, and rewardeth transgressors.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "As a dog returneth to his vomit, so a fool returneth to his folly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Seest thou a man wise in his own conceit? there is more hope of a fool than of him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "The slothful man saith, There is a lion in the way; a lion is in the streets.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "As the door turneth upon his hinges, so doth the slothful upon his bed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "The slothful hideth his hand in his bosom; it grieveth him to bring it again to his mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "The sluggard is wiser in his own conceit than seven men that can render a reason.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "He that passeth by, and meddleth with strife belonging not to him, is like one that taketh a dog by the ears.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "As a mad man who casteth firebrands, arrows, and death,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "So is the man that deceiveth his neighbour, and saith, Am not I in sport?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Where no wood is, there the fire goeth out: so where there is no talebearer, the strife ceaseth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "As coals are to burning coals, and wood to fire; so is a contentious man to kindle strife.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "The words of a talebearer are as wounds, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Burning lips and a wicked heart are like a potsherd covered with silver dross.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "He that hateth dissembleth with his lips, and layeth up deceit within him;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "When he speaketh fair, believe him not: for there are seven abominations in his heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "Whose hatred is covered by deceit, his wickedness shall be shewed before the whole congregation.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Whoso diggeth a pit shall fall therein: and he that rolleth a stone, it will return upon him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:26:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "A lying tongue hateth those that are afflicted by it; and a flattering mouth worketh ruin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 26:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:26:28"
      }
    }
  ],
